# SkiaSharp's .so comes from the NuGet package with freetype, libjpeg and libpng already
# compiled in: that is the only way SkiaSharp is distributed, and there is no variant linked
# against the system libraries.
#
# The cost is real and is stated here rather than hidden: a vulnerability in one of those
# three is NOT fixed by updating Debian. It is fixed by updating the SkiaSharp package and
# rebuilding this .deb.
#
# This file lists the one thing that cannot be fixed. Everything else lintian used to flag -
# unstripped symbols, non-standard permissions, a changelog with the wrong name for a native
# package, missing man pages - was fixed in pack.sh, not silenced here.
observer: embedded-library freetype [usr/lib/observer/dashboard/libSkiaSharp.so]
observer: embedded-library libjpeg [usr/lib/observer/dashboard/libSkiaSharp.so]
observer: embedded-library libpng [usr/lib/observer/dashboard/libSkiaSharp.so]
